1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,022
The better question arrived in the evening, on the back of a report.

2
00:00:04,022 --> 00:00:08,176
Which item on the list actually changes a decision?

3
00:00:08,176 --> 00:00:14,720
The number of complaints was a score; the quality of one private note was a factor.

4
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:18,765
“A city is not a unit,” Maya said.

5
00:00:18,765 --> 00:00:27,609
“It is a league of small arrangements.” Her hand moved across the page and stopped at a single line.

6
00:00:27,609 --> 00:00:38,747
The club had spread its stuff across the table: a map, a gas bill, a cover from an old magazine, and a photograph of a soldier.

7
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:44,382
The group had no property, no estate, and no independent income.

8
00:00:44,382 --> 00:00:48,046
Their pride was the only capital they had.

9
00:00:48,046 --> 00:00:52,356
“Where is the conflict?” Lin asked.

10
00:00:52,356 --> 00:00:57,870
“It is in the distance between what we measure and what people need.”

11
00:00:57,870 --> 00:01:01,680
Mark the limit, then adjust the shape.

12
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:15,693
A voluntary member of the committee, a captain of the rowing team, and a student who studied philosophy all said the same thing: the decline of trust had a consequence that no chart showed.

13
00:01:15,693 --> 00:01:21,637
The old colonial map was still on the wall under a protective sheet of plastic.

14
00:01:21,637 --> 00:01:29,701
Restraint, not enthusiasm, would decide whether they could keep their idea alive.

15
00:01:29,701 --> 00:01:35,880
The climax came on a Thursday, when the student union demanded a decision.

16
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:43,874
Lin wanted to clone the successful west-gate experiment; Maya wanted to keep the club's independence.

17
00:01:43,874 --> 00:01:47,533
“That is not a choice,” she said.

18
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:57,527
“That is a descent into the same mistake.” Anything else, she thought, would be pride wearing a new coat.

19
00:01:57,527 --> 00:02:00,042
They chose a third path.

20
00:02:00,042 --> 00:02:14,385
The report would change one line: from “cover every gate” to “ask a better question at every gate.” But the rate of progress was slower than anyone liked, and no one could explain why.

21
00:02:14,385 --> 00:02:20,699
A guy from the city desk laughed at their absolute rule, and then wrote it down.

22
00:02:20,699 --> 00:02:25,869
“Your notes are the only thing holding this together,” Lin said.

23
00:02:25,869 --> 00:02:41,802
“Each member has to share them, and that is an opportunity, not a burden.” Until the summer, a voluntary team would keep the notes public; after that, the arrangement would have to stand on its own.

24
00:02:41,802 --> 00:02:47,822
“Yeah,” Maya said, “that is worth the risk.”
